Tests for `parse_template`, the template string parser in the steno crate. The parser converts domain syntax — literal text, `%`-prefixed operators, structural braces, escapes, repeats, and computed expressions — into a `Chunk` enum that downstream code consumes. This test file is the Rust port of `test/parse.test.ts` and covers the template half.

The parser recognizes: single-digit landings (`%0`–`%9`), fixed operators (`%d` dcount, `%t` type-slot, `%b` body-break, `%p` pattern), repeats with optional separators (`%[sep | body %]`), computed linear expressions `%(ad±b)` where `d` is a placeholder, and end-landings `%<N>`. Structural braces become `Chunk::Brace` entries; backslash escapes handle brace, percent, backslash, and backtick as literals, while `\n` and `\t` become `Chunk::Newline` and `Chunk::Tab`. A pipe `|` is literal outside repeats. Multi-digit landings parse as single digit plus literal remainder.

Tests validate: primitives (literals, operators, braces), repeats (with and without separators, nested), computed expressions in all linear forms, escape sequences, and error cases covering unknown operators, unterminated constructs, malformed expressions, and invalid end-landings.